The CUDA decode matvec (forge_qmatmul_q81 / forge_quant_q81 in ops/gen/gpu_gen.py) follows the design of
ggml-cuda's mul_mat_vec_q (mmvq.cu, vecdotq.cuh): q8_1-quantised activations, dp4a dot products against
the GGUF-encoded weight blocks, and a warp per output column. The code is a FORGE implementation.
modelfile/include/forge/import/quant_recipe.hpp: its "llama" recipe is a port of llama_tensor_get_type() from
src/llama-quant.cpp (commit bc428e407a52bd3e21b5985cabeef57cdff9bc4a; the ported line ranges are listed in the file).
modelfile/include/forge/import/tokenizer_import.hpp: the table of pre-tokenizer names and their split regexes
(gguf_pre_regexes) and the conventions for "bert" vocabularies follow llama.cpp's tokenizer;
they were written from memory of it and have not been diffed against the original.

