Intrinsic databases (ops/intrinsics/*.json, and the wrappers ops/gen/intrin_gen.py generates from them at build time)
The databases hold the names, signatures, required target features and immediate-operand constraints of compiler
intrinsics. They are derived by the build scripts next to them (build_*_db.py), not typed in, from:

  x86.json, loongarch.json, mips.json, ppc.json, s390x.json, wasm.json
      the intrinsic headers of clang 23 (<immintrin.h>, <lsxintrin.h>, <lasxintrin.h>, <msa.h>, <altivec.h>,
      <vecintrin.h>, <wasm_simd128.h>). Each of these headers states: "Part of the LLVM Project, under the Apache
      License v2.0 with LLVM Exceptions. See https://llvm.org/LICENSE.txt for license information."
      SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
  arm.json
      <arm_acle.h>, <arm_sve.h>, <arm_neon_sve_bridge.h>, <arm_sme.h> of clang 23 (same statement, Apache-2.0 WITH
      LLVM-exception) and <arm_neon.h>, which clang generates and which carries the MIT permission notice (without a
      copyright line) instead.
  riscv.json, riscv_policy.json
      The prototype lists of the RISC-V Vector intrinsics specification, https://github.com/riscv-non-isa/rvv-intrinsic-doc
      (auto-generated/**/intrinsic_funcs.adoc), each prototype compiled against clang 23's builtins; the scalar helpers
      come from clang's <riscv_bitmanip.h> and <riscv_crypto.h> (Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception).
      LICENCE OF rvv-intrinsic-doc: NOT ESTABLISHED. Neither ops/intrinsics/build_riscv_db.py, ops/README.md nor the
      generated databases record it, the copy the databases were built from is not in this repository, and it could
      not be read from the project when this notice was written (2026-11-12: its README.md names no licence and no
      LICENSE file was found at the root of its main branch). This statement stands as written: the project's owner
      decided on 2026-11-13 not to pursue the question for the time being.

No header text is copied into the databases: what they hold is each intrinsic's name and prototype. The attribution
is given because the lists as a whole are taken from those sources.

