Test fixtures (not part of any built library or program)
  tests/data/tokenizer   Tokenizers trained by tests/data/tokenizer/make_fixtures.py on the corpus in that script, with
      the Hugging Face `tokenizers` package (Apache-2.0) and the `sentencepiece` package (Apache-2.0); the .gguf files
      were written with the `gguf` package of llama.cpp (MIT). The files are outputs of those tools on FORGE's own
      text; they contain no vocabulary, normalization table or model of a third party (the SentencePiece charsmap in
      spm_unigram_charsmap.model is compiled from a rule table defined in the script, not from nmt_nfkc).
      goldens.json records what those packages return for the corpus.
  tests/data/chat_template   make_goldens.py holds chat templates of published models (ChatML, Qwen 2.5 / 3, Llama 2 / 3,
      Mistral, Gemma, Phi-3, DeepSeek, Zephyr), written out from memory of the models' tokenizer_config.json
      files and not diffed against them. The originals belong to the model publishers and are under each model's
      licence; they are used here only as test input for the template renderer. goldens.json is the rendering of them
      by the `jinja2` package (BSD licence, per its package metadata).

